ce/day/time, and timezone if the device timezone is unavailable or likely wrong.",'- For result destination, say: "By default, answers go to the chat. Anywhere else you want the results?" Offer these choices: "Just chat is good", "Email", "Slack", and "Spreadsheet".','- Keep answer choices concise and easy to scan. Use short labels like "Daily briefing", "Inbox digest", "Update spreadsheet", "Every weekday", "Slack DM", or "Email summary", not full-sentence options.',"- Make choices context-aware using the user wording, current page, connected apps, and likely workflow intent. Every question already has a built-in freeform field for anything not covered.","- Ask another follow-up only if a required account, source, destination, or schedule detail is still missing after discovery and setup.",'- When ready, use save_skill with kind="workflow", self-contained workflow instructions, requested schedules, and the user timezone when relevant.']),skill:ua("Help me create a reusable skill. Briefly explain how skills work in Polar, then ask me three quick questions with suggested answers and a custom option so you can draft the guidance.",["Polar skill setup guidance:","- Goal: help the user define reusable instructions Polar can load when relevant to the current work, or when the user invokes the skill manually.","- When answering this question, explain that skills are generally for personal preferences in certain tasks or sites, extra context or instructions for recurring work, and improving cases where Polar was not doing a good job. Do not mention workflows; the user is trying to create a regular skill.","- Use ask_question for three quick questions: when Polar should consider the skill relevant, what preference/context/instruction Polar should apply, and what better behavior should look like.","- For each question, offer a few concise suggested answers; every question already has a built-in freeform field for custom responses.",'- Make suggestions context-aware when possible, using short labels like "Writing voice", "Gmail triage", "PR review style", "Linear context", or "Report format".','- After the user answers, draft the skill with reasonable defaults, infer a short kebab-case command name, and save it with kind="skill".'])},hM={"bar-chart":Jg,"book-open":Bg,bot:Fg,bug:Vg,building:Wg,calendar:Ug,"check-check":Qg,"check-circle":cm,clipboard:t0,code:r0,"file-check":c0,"file-text":lm,globe:da,home:d0,inbox:h0,lightbulb:m0,mail:y0,megaphone:x0,message:w0,plane:C0,presentation:E0,receipt:A0,scan:Ll,search:Ll,shield:D0,sparkles:vd,tag:B0,ticket:W0,users:Hm,utensils:Q0};function zp({icon:n,brandDomains:e,className:t,monochrome:r=!1}){const s=hM[n]??vd,i=h.jsx(s,{className:t}),o=$p(e)[0];return o?h.jsx(Fp,{domain:o,className:t,fallback:i,monochrome:r}):i}function Vp(n){const[e,t]=b.useState(null),r=b.useRef(null),s=b.useCallback((i,o,a)=>{if(r.current!==null)return;r.current=i;const l=ua(o.prompt,o.system_reminder_lines);t(i),(async()=>{try{await n({text:l.visibleText,userMessageContent:[{type:"text",text:l.visibleText}],hiddenContext:l.hiddenContext,modeOverride:ct.getState().draftAgentMode,fastResponses:ct.getState().draftFastResponses})&&(a==null||a())}catch(c){console.error("Failed to launch catalog query:",c)}finally{r.current===i&&(r.current=null),t(c=>c===i?null:c)}})()},[n]);return{launchingId:e,launch:s}}const Ju=3;function pM(){return Math.floor(Date.now()/864e5)%ld}const Gu="flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl border border-subtle px-3 py-1.5 text-xs text-customNeutral-150 transition-colors hover:bg-hover-fill hover:text-customNeutral-50 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-primary disabled:cursor-default disabled:opacity-60 disabled:hover:bg-transparent";function mM({onSend:n}){const{launchingId:e,launch:t}=Vp(n),{data:r,isLoading:s}=Um(!0,Ju,pM()),i=(r==null?void 0:r.suggestions)??[],o=b.useCallback(a=>{Xn("suggestion_chip_clicked",{suggestion_id:a.id,suggestion_hook:a.hook,suggestion_cluster:a